        <div id="post-743" class="post-743 post type-post hentry category-ioc category-wpf">

          <div class="post-header">
           <h3 class="post-title"><a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2009/10/registering-wpf-views-with-windsor-fluent-api/" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Registering WPF &#8220;Views&#8221; with Windsor Fluent API">Registering WPF &#8220;Views&#8221; with Windsor Fluent API</a></h3>
           <p class="post-date">
            <span class="month">Oct</span>
            <span class="day">26</span>
           </p>
           <p class="post-author">
            <span class="info">Posted by <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/author/cromwellryan/" title="Posts by cromwellryan ">cromwellryan</a> in <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/ioc/" title="View all posts in IoC" rel="category tag">IoC</a>, <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/category/wpf/" title="View all posts in WPF" rel="category tag">WPF</a> | <a href="http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/2009/10/registering-wpf-views-with-windsor-fluent-api/#respond" class="comments"  title="Comment on Registering WPF &#8220;Views&#8221; with Windsor Fluent API"><span class="dsq-postid" rel="743 http://blog.cromwellhaus.com/index.php/2009/10/registering-wpf-views-with-windsor-fluent-api/">View Comments</span></a>              </span>
           </p>
          </div>

          <div class="post-content clearfix">
          <p>I’ve had this nagging issue for some time now with WPF views that are registered for an interface.&#160; The Views themselves are WPF UserControls: namespace SomeApp.Views { public partial class SearchView : UserControl, ISearchView { public SearchView() { InitializeComponent(); } private void InitializeComponent() { throw new NotImplementedException(); } } } &#160; I would love to [...]</p>

